  "expectedTreatmentHtml": "<p><strong>Oxygen:</strong> SpO₂ 95% — borderline. NC 2 LPM if working, or hold (not below 94%). Once they determine shock, they should give NRB or at least 6LPM NC.</p><p><strong>Aspirin 324 mg</strong> — indicated, no allergy.</p><p><strong style=\"color:#9D0208\">Nitroglycerin: CONTRAINDICATED</strong> — BP 86/58 below 90 systolic. Inferior MI with bradycardia + hypotension is classic right-ventricular involvement; nitro can crash BP.</p><p><strong>Position:</strong> supine or position of comfort.</p><p><strong>Transport:</strong> unstable — load and go, ALS intercept critical, possible cath lab activation.</p>",
  "pitfallsHtml": "<p>• <strong>Giving nitro despite BP under 90</strong> — critical thinking failure, dangerous intervention<br>• Overdoing oxygen on a 95% patient<br>• Missing the bradycardia + hypotension pattern (inferior MI)<br>• Treating this as \"just chest pain\"<br>• Slow scene time — this is a STEMI</p>",
