  "expectedTreatmentHtml": "<p><strong>Spinal motion restriction:</strong> full SMR (spinal motion restriction) — C-collar, log-roll to backboard, towel rolls, straps. <em>Critical fail if not done.</em></p><p><strong>Oxygen:</strong> SpO₂ 96% — NRB 10-12 LPM acceptable.</p><p><strong>Pelvic binder</strong> — unstable pelvis with hypotension. CRITICAL FAIL IF DOES NOT, Apply commercial binder or improvise with sheet at level of greater trochanters.</p><p><strong>Treat for shock</strong> — keep warm, supine.</p><p><strong>Transport:</strong> UNSTABLE — load and go. Trauma center. ALS intercept.</p>",
  "pitfallsHtml": "<p>• <strong>Letting patient move himself</strong> — major spinal mechanism<br>• Missing the unstable pelvis (hypotension + fall = think pelvis)<br>• Not assessing PMS bilaterally<br>• Not applying pelvic binder<br>• Skipping the posterior assessment during log-roll<br>• Forgetting to ask about loss of consciousness</p>",
