  "expectedTreatmentHtml": "<p><strong>Scene safety:</strong> verify PD secured before approach.</p><p><strong>Oxygen:</strong> NRB 15 LPM. <em>Critical fail if not provided.</em></p><p><strong>OCCLUSIVE DRESSING (3-sided / vented chest seal)</strong> — for sucking chest wound. Tape on three sides only OR commercial vented seal. <em>If a 4-sided seal is applied, monitor for tension pneumothorax — burp the seal if patient deteriorates.</em></p><p><strong>Position:</strong> position of comfort (often semi-Fowler's). Affected side down if tolerated.</p><p><strong>Reassess frequently</strong> for tension pneumothorax: rising HR, falling BP, JVD, tracheal deviation, severe SOB.</p><p><strong>Transport:</strong> UNSTABLE — load and go. Trauma center. ALS intercept.</p>",
  "pitfallsHtml": "<p>• <strong>Sealing the chest wound completely without venting</strong> — risk of tension pneumothorax<br>• Not log-rolling to look for additional wounds<br>• Forgetting to reassess for tension pneumothorax development<br>• Approaching scene before PD secures<br>• Removing penetrating object (don't — though here the knife is gone already)<br>• Slow scene time</p>",
