  "expectedTreatmentHtml": "<p><strong>Spinal motion restriction:</strong> peds with significant mechanism — apply C-collar (peds size), full SMR.</p><p><strong>Oxygen:</strong> SpO₂ 97% — NRB 10-12 LPM.</p><p><strong>Splint the closed right femur fracture</strong> — pediatric traction splint if it fits; otherwise rigid splint secured to the board. Check PMS before and after.</p><p><strong>Bandage</strong> abrasions.</p><p><strong>Treat for shock:</strong> children compensate well then crash suddenly. Tachy + cool/diaphoretic = shock until proven otherwise.</p><p><strong>Family-centered care</strong> — communicate with mom on arrival, allow brief contact if practical.</p><p><strong>Transport:</strong> UNSTABLE — load and go. Pediatric trauma center.</p>",
  "pitfallsHtml": "<p>• <strong>Underestimating pediatric shock</strong> — kids compensate then crash<br>• Forgetting age-appropriate sizing for C-collar and splints<br>• CRITICAL FAIL, not splinting, big possible bleed<br>• Not communicating calmly with the child<br>• Waiting unnecessarily for mom (arranging for her to follow/meet)<br>• Slow scene time on a load-and-go peds trauma<br>• Skipping the posterior assessment</p>",
